    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0982" n="1940" xml:id="pg1940"/>

                <head>No. 65.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hubbard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 4,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 117 of December
                    28, 1887, concerning the desire of Japan to enter into a convention for the
                    abolition of tonnage or equivalent charges on merchant vessels plying between
                    the United States and Japan.</p>
                <p>A copy of your dispatch was at once communicated to the Secretary of the
                    Treasury, a copy of whose reply, dated the 1st instant, is herewith transmitted.
                    To enable full consideration of the subject and a definite reply to be made to
                    the inquiry of the Japanese minister for foreign affairs as to the future status
                    of Japanese and other vessels proceeding to the United States respecting
                    navigation charges, it will be necessary to ascertain the amount of tax or
                    taxes, equivalent to tonnage or lighthouse dues, imposed in Japan on American
                    vessels.</p>
                <p>You will therefore take occasion to obtain this information, which should be set
                    forth in detail, if possible, in accordance with the suggestion of the Secretary
                    of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d627-a1.xml" xpointer="d627-a1"/>
            </div>
